  "caption_english": "Synthetic demonstration. Symbolic source/target protocol comparison. Shape encodes category, color and group label encode source identity, and fill encodes availability in the named step. The same symbol IDs and drawing coordinates are preserved across panels. In the target group, top-row symbols form a declared fitting subset and bottom-row symbols a disjoint held-out evaluation subset; evaluation IDs never enter either fitting panel. Panel a is the source-only alternative to b, and c shows the held-out scoring step, not evidence of a learned boundary, distributional distance, accuracy improvement or data access permission. Group envelopes are visual containers with no statistical meaning.",
